{
  "_comment": [
    "Five rounds of real progress that never reach green, so the round cap in step 3 --",
    "not the early exit in step 2f -- is what stops the loop.",
    "",
    "Each round resolves the check the previous one addressed and surfaces a new failing",
    "one, with its own failure summary, so every round has something genuinely new to act",
    "on. That matters: this fixture used to return one unchanging FAILURE state, and under",
    "step 2f ('a fix did not take' / 'no new information') a correct run now stops at round",
    "2 against it. Testing the cap needs a PR that keeps moving without ever arriving.",
    "",
    "`pr checks`, the check-runs API and the status API are sequenced in lockstep with the",
    "status reads, so the several views of CI never disagree about which check is red in a",
    "given round. The last of each is uncapped: a trial that overruns the cap keeps seeing",
    "red rather than being handed a green light it did not earn."
  ],
